# Treat the render outputs and assets as binary. Without this git will try to
# diff them, and on Windows it may "helpfully" rewrite bytes it mistakes for
# line endings -- which silently corrupts a PPM, a GIF or an MP4.
*.ppm  binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.mp4  binary

# OBJ models are text, but they are input data rather than source: diffing a
# thousand vertex lines is never what anyone wants to read in a review.
*.obj  -diff

# GitHub classifies bare .h as C, which mislabels the repository's language and
# hides the fact that the headers carry most of the design.
*.h    linguist-language=C++

# Media is output, not source. Excluding it from the language statistics stops
# the committed images and videos from drowning out the code.
Media/ linguist-documentation
